L4-E6: FAULT HANDLING OF BOARD A'S FRONT END U2 (LM5176), FINDINGS B-1, B-2 AND B-4 (l4e6_fault_handling.py, MESHSAT-1357).
PROTOTYPE DESIGN: nothing bought, built, powered or measured; no generator, registry, rendered page or L4-E4/L4-E5 record
edited. Basis per figure: MAKER (document, page), NETLIST, MODELED, INFERRED (method stated), ASSUMPTION; INCONCLUSIVE
where no held document gives the figure.

0. REPRODUCTIONS BEFORE ANY RESULT
   0a l4e4_limits.py re-run in a child process reproduces l4e4_limits.out byte for byte (sha256/16 f68bf6951a6361ca): yes
   0b l4e5_source_control.py re-run in a child process reproduces l4e5_source_control.out byte for byte (sha256/16 f9c98ec5c43ada0e): yes
   0c r11_dep.py re-run in a child process reproduces r11_dep.out byte for byte (sha256/16 f9d2c6f23fab3edc): yes
   0d l4e4_limits.compute() run here renders l4e4_limits.out byte for byte: yes (band(), R11 8 mOhm and its 7 mOhm alternative taken from it)
   0e r11_dep.main() run here (locals captured by l4e4_limits.run_main_captured) prints r11_dep.out byte for byte: yes
      (stage(), peak_b(), fet_tj(), Figure 8's readings, the generator's VBUS20 bank figures and their per-can scaling taken from it);
      r11_dep.py's FET loss relations, restated here once, reprint all nine of its section 4 FET lines byte for byte: yes
   L4-E5's figures read from its reproduced output: the pin path 5.016 A in board current, 5.095 A through R11, between 26.50 and
   27.24 V; V-A07's threshold 0.071 A; H3's highest U3 board current 1.793 A at 9 V and 2.323 A at 12 V; the 7 mOhm consequence
   (C2904239, 8.300 A) checked equal to L4-E4's alternative. The vehicle entry's 6.15 A from r11_dep.out (gen_sch_e.py _VEH_T)
   LM5176 sheet sha256/16 98191bec36d43771; Coilcraft XAL1010 (Document 804-1, revised 02/25/26) and XAL1510 (Document 947-1, revised 05/04/26) pinned

1. WHAT BOARD A CARRIES AND WHAT THE MAKERS PRINT
   NETLIST: R12 '5mOhm 1% 2512 (CS)' from FE_CS to GND, U2's cycle-by-cycle sense (lcsc_fill.py C500739, LR2512D-3W-5mR-1%)
   NETLIST: Q3 and Q4 sources (pins 1 to 3) on FE_CS: R12 carries the low-side switches' current
   NETLIST: the CS filter R150, R151 '100R 1%' into U2 pins 16 and 15, C123 '1n' across
   NETLIST: R119 '100k (MODE: CCM)' from FE_MODE (U2 pin 4) to FE_VCC (pin 23): MODE to VCC
   NETLIST: C147 '680p' on FE_SLOPE (the slope capacitor)
   NETLIST: C7 '4.7u' on FE_SS (the soft start)
   NETLIST: L1 '10uH XAL1010-103ME (Isat 17.5 A)'
   NETLIST: U2 is the HTSSOP-28 (LM5176PWPR): the HTSSOP current-limit rows apply
   MAKER SNVSAI1D (LM5176, rev. D, August 2021):
     p.13: the inductor current is sensed through ONE resistor in series with the low-side MOSFETs (R12) and monitored for the
       cycle-by-cycle limit; without hiccup the controller stays in that limit until the overload is removed
     p.16 7.3.5: boost, the low-side switch turns off for the rest of the cycle when CS-CSG exceeds VCS(BOOST); buck, the high-side
       switch skips a cycle while the sensed valley stays above VCS(BUCK). p.7 (HTSSOP): VCS(BOOST) 100 / 120 / 140 mV, VCS(BUCK)
       66 / 80 / 94 mV, IOFFSET(CS/CSG) 19 uA (MAX column), gmSLOPE 2 uS; p.5: CS, CSG at most 0.3 V
     p.17 7.3.5: hiccup shuts the controller down after 128 CONSECUTIVE CYCLE-BY-CYCLE LIMITS and releases SS after 4000 clock cycles;
       p.16 7.3.4 and p.17 7.3.6: the AVERAGE limit acts by discharging SS through its gm amplifier, so it never counts as a
       cycle-by-cycle limit: hiccup does not act on the highest permitted current the average limit sets (INFERRED from the two)
     p.3 and p.20: 1.38 V < MODE < 2.22 V selects CCM with hiccup (RMODE 93.1 kOhm to AGND); 2.6 V < MODE < VCC, or MODE to VCC,
       no hiccup; MODE is latched at start-up. p.7: IMODE 17 / 20 / 23 uA
     p.6: ISS 3.75 / 5 / 6.35 uA, VREF 0.788 / 0.800 / 0.812 V, fSW 175 / 200 / 225 kHz at RT 40 k
     p.24 8.2.2.7: the CS resistor is sized from the application's own currents (Equation 23, 80 mV / IOUT(MAX); Equation 24,
       120 mV / IL(PEAK)); 8.2.2.8 Equation 26, CSLOPE = gmSLOPE x L1 / (RSENSE x ACS), ACS 5 (its example): 800 pF at the drawn
       5 mOhm, C147 680 pF; 'a current mode loop is stable with half the dead-beat slope'
   MAKER Coilcraft XAL1010-103ME (Document 804-1, p.1): Isat 17.5 A typical at 25 C (note 5: 30 % inductance drop), Irms 15.5 A at
     40 K rise, L +-20 %; temperature derating is a link ('Click for temperature derating information'), and p.3's 'Typical L
     vs Current' is one 25 C curve: Isat at the part's temperature is NOT HELD (C-5) -> INCONCLUSIVE
   MAKER Coilcraft XAL1510-103ME (Document 947-1, p.1; board E's tracker inductor): 10 uH, DCR 9.00 mOhm max, Isat 26.3 A typical
     at 25 C, Irms 16 / 22 A (20 / 40 K); the same derating link, not held
   INFERRED here: the CS filter's lag 222 ns (R150 + R151 at +1 %, C123 at +10 %, an ASSUMPTION: the netlist prints '1n');
     the CSG offset 1.9 mV (IOFFSET over one 100 Ohm), added against each end of the limits; the comparator's own delay is NOT
     PRINTED (INCONCLUSIVE), so B-1 states the delay its headroom admits

